01:23:53,333 --> 01:23:59,333
The New World is a 2005 historical romantic drama film written and directed by Terrence Malick, depicting the founding of the Jamestown, Virginia,
settlement and inspired by the historical figures Captain John Smith, Pocahontas of the Powhatan tribe, and Englishman John Rolfe.

11
01:32:16,666 --> 01:32:22,666
It is the fourth feature film written and directed by Malick.

12
01:40:40,000 --> 01:40:46,000
The cast includes Colin Farrell, Q'orianka Kilcher, Christopher Plummer, Christian Bale, August
Schellenberg, Wes Studi, David Thewlis, Yorick van Wageningen and John Savage.

13
01:49:03,333 --> 01:49:09,333
The production team includes director of photography Emmanuel Lubezki, producer Sarah Green, production designer Jack Fisk, costume
designer Jacqueline West, composer James Horner and film editors Richard Chew, Hank Corwin, Saar Klein and Mark Yoshikawa.

14
01:57:26,666 --> 01:57:32,666
The New World was a box-office failure even though it received many award nominations
for Lubezki's cinematography, Kilcher's acting and Horner's score.

15
02:05:50,000 --> 02:05:56,000
The film was initially met with an only mildly positive critical response, although
several critics later ranked it as one of the best films of the decade.

16
02:14:13,333 --> 02:14:19,333
The film explores themes of native american, native american
attack, interracial romance, colonialism, virginia.

17
02:22:36,666 --> 02:22:42,666
The tone is emotional.
